Short:        Micro Emacs (mg), a small fast Emacs
Author:       mg authors (troglobit/mg); Amiga port by Per Weijnitz
Uploader:     @UPLOADER@
Type:         text/edit
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Distribution: Aminet
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.0 or newer, 68000 or better

mg is a small, fast Emacs for the Shell window: GNU Emacs keys and
commands for everyday editing in one 200 KB program, no support files.
This is mg @UPSTREAM@ (https://github.com/troglobit/mg) ported to AmigaOS:

- raw console I/O, cursor and function keys, Shift+cursor for start/end
  of line and page up/down, F1/Help for quick help
- Amiga path names (Work:dir/file) in prompts and completion
- dired, the directory editor, with its own listing (no ls needed)
- saved files keep their protection bits (s, e...) and comment
- the window size from the console, ISO-8859-1 text
- runs on a 68000 (A500) as well as on faster CPUs; tested on AmigaOS 3.2

Left out, because AmigaOS cannot run programs the Unix way: shell
commands and pipes, compile/grep, cscope/ctags, regex search.

Install: copy mg to C:, see README.txt.

Source and issues: https://github.com/perweij/mg-amiga
Built from the source there by GitHub Actions with m68k-amigaos-gcc and
clib2.  mg is public domain; LICENSES.txt lists the notices of the parts
under other licences.
